% Test cases for the automatic external defibrillator policy (aeds.le):
% synthetic claims, one per criterion of LCD L33690 for the wearable and
% the nonwearable defibrillator, and for the diagnosis code Policy Article
% A52458 requires on the claim. Findings are recorded as the treating
% practitioner's, a medical reviewer's or the Council's; a finding nobody
% made leaves the answer conditional. The wearable defibrillator is rented
% (the first month's claim is shown); the nonwearable one is a purchase.
% One scenario is modelled on the Council's decision M-13-751 (Zoll LifeCor
% Corporation, 2013), which denied a wearable defibrillator delivered to a
% hospital inpatient three days before discharge: the hospital is not a
% home.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base aeds cases includes these resources:
    aeds.

the knowledge base aeds cases includes:

query pay is:
    which claim is payable.

query rn is:
    which claim is reasonable and necessary.

query stage is:
    the query fails at which section.

query flip is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        claim 1 is payable.

% A complete first-month claim for a wearable defibrillator (K0606) by
% criterion 1: a documented ventricular fibrillation, no transient cause,
% the diagnosis code I49.01 on the claim, the standard written order
% communicated before the date of service, the delivery and its proof.
scenario wearable_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the wearable defibrillator.
    the HCPCS code of the wearable defibrillator is "K0606".
    the wearable defibrillator is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the medical record of Ann documents ventricular fibrillation.
    the finding transient cause excluded about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "no electrolyte disturbance, drug toxicity or infection at the time of the episode".
    the diagnosis code of Ann is "I49.01".
    the order for the wearable defibrillator is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the wearable defibrillator is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the wearable defibrillator includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the wearable defibrillator includes order date.
    the order for the wearable defibrillator includes description of the item.
    the order for the wearable defibrillator includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the wearable defibrillator includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the wearable defibrillator was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the wearable defibrillator was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the wearable defibrillator.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

% The other wearable routes: a sustained tachyarrhythmia of 45 seconds
% (claim 1); a dilated cardiomyopathy with an ejection fraction of 0.30
% (claim 2); an implanted defibrillator that requires explantation (claim
% 3); and a tachyarrhythmia of 20 seconds, too short (claim 4).
scenario wearable_routes is:
    claim 1 is for the first vest.
    the HCPCS code of the first vest is "K0606".
    the first vest is furnished to Ben.
    the medical record of Ben documents a sustained ventricular tachyarrhythmia lasting 45 seconds.
    the finding transient cause excluded about Ben is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    claim 2 is for the second vest.
    the HCPCS code of the second vest is "K0606".
    the second vest is furnished to Cy.
    the medical record of Cy documents dilated cardiomyopathy.
    the measured left ventricular ejection fraction of Cy is 0.30.
    claim 3 is for the third vest.
    the HCPCS code of the third vest is "K0606".
    the third vest is furnished to Dee.
    the previously implanted defibrillator of Dee requires explantation.
    claim 4 is for the fourth vest.
    the HCPCS code of the fourth vest is "K0606".
    the fourth vest is furnished to Eve.
    the medical record of Eve documents a sustained ventricular tachyarrhythmia lasting 20 seconds.
    the finding transient cause excluded about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 2 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 3 is reasonable and necessary"].

% Criterion 1 fails on the exclusion: the fibrillation occurred within 48
% hours of an acute myocardial infarction.
scenario fibrillation_during_infarction is:
    claim 1 is for the wearable defibrillator.
    the HCPCS code of the wearable defibrillator is "K0606".
    the wearable defibrillator is furnished to Fay.
    the residence of Fay is private residence.
    the medical record of Fay documents ventricular fibrillation.
    the finding transient cause excluded about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the ventricular dysrhythmia of Fay occurred within 48 hours of an acute myocardial infarction.
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at question"].

% Criterion 3 fails on the threshold: an ejection fraction of 0.40.
scenario ejection_fraction_too_high is:
    claim 1 is for the wearable defibrillator.
    the HCPCS code of the wearable defibrillator is "K0606".
    the wearable defibrillator is furnished to Gus.
    the medical record of Gus documents myocardial infarction.
    the measured left ventricular ejection fraction of Gus is 0.40.
    rn expects answers [].

% The Council finds the tachyarrhythmia had a reversible cause the LCD
% names: the finding is unsupported.
scenario transient_cause_council is:
    claim 1 is for the wearable defibrillator.
    the HCPCS code of the wearable defibrillator is "K0606".
    the wearable defibrillator is furnished to Hal.
    the medical record of Hal documents a sustained ventricular tachyarrhythmia lasting 40 seconds.
    the finding transient cause excluded about Hal is unsupported, according to the Council, because "the hospital record attributes the ventricular tachycardia to severe hypokalemia corrected before discharge, a reversible cause the LCD names".
    rn expects answers [].

% Modelled on Council decision M-13-751: a wearable defibrillator delivered
% to a hospital inpatient three days before discharge, with an ejection
% fraction of 0.35 and a cardiomyopathy in the record. The criteria are
% met, but the hospital is not a home: the claim fails at applicability.
scenario delivered_in_hospital is:
    claim 1 is for the wearable defibrillator.
    the HCPCS code of the wearable defibrillator is "K0606".
    the wearable defibrillator is furnished to Ida.
    the residence of Ida is hospital.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2010-09-17.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the medical record of Ida documents dilated cardiomyopathy.
    the measured left ventricular ejection fraction of Ida is 0.35.
    the diagnosis code of Ida is "I42.0".
    the order for the wearable defibrillator is dated 2010-09-17.
    the order for the wearable defibrillator is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the wearable defibrillator includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the wearable defibrillator includes order date.
    the order for the wearable defibrillator includes description of the item.
    the order for the wearable defibrillator includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the wearable defibrillator includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the wearable defibrillator was communicated to the supplier on 2010-09-17.
    the wearable defibrillator was delivered on 2010-09-17.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the wearable defibrillator.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at applicability"].

% A nonwearable defibrillator (E0617) by condition 4 with implantation
% contraindicated: coronary artery disease, an infarction on 2025-11-01, an
% electrophysiologic study on 2026-01-15 that induced tachycardia, an
% ejection fraction of 0.30, the order on 2026-02-20 — both more than 28
% days after the infarction; the diagnosis code I25.2 on the claim.
scenario nonwearable_condition_4_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the defibrillator.
    the HCPCS code of the defibrillator is "E0617".
    the defibrillator is furnished to Jo.
    the residence of Jo is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the medical record of Jo documents coronary artery disease.
    the medical record of Jo documents myocardial infarction.
    the qualifying myocardial infarction of Jo occurred on 2025-11-01.
    the measured left ventricular ejection fraction of Jo is 0.30.
    the electrophysiologic study of Jo was performed on 2026-01-15.
    the electrophysiologic study of Jo induced sustained ventricular tachycardia or fibrillation.
    the finding implantation surgery contraindicated about Jo is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "active endocarditis".
    the diagnosis code of Jo is "I25.2".
    the order for the defibrillator is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the defibrillator is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the defibrillator includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the defibrillator includes order date.
    the order for the defibrillator includes description of the item.
    the order for the defibrillator includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the defibrillator includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the defibrillator was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the defibrillator was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the defibrillator.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

% Condition 5: an infarction with an ejection fraction of 0.25, with (claim
% 2) and without (claim 1) an exclusion in the record — a bypass graft two
% months ago; condition 7: a nonischemic dilated cardiomyopathy diagnosed
% eight months before the order, NYHA class III, ejection fraction 0.30
% (claim 3); condition 6 with NYHA class IV, admitted by condition 8 (claim
% 4). Implantation surgery contraindicated for all.
scenario nonwearable_conditions_5_to_8 is:
    claim 1 is for the first defibrillator.
    the HCPCS code of the first defibrillator is "E0617".
    the first defibrillator is furnished to Kim.
    the medical record of Kim documents myocardial infarction.
    the measured left ventricular ejection fraction of Kim is 0.25.
    the finding implantation surgery contraindicated about Kim is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    claim 2 is for the second defibrillator.
    the HCPCS code of the second defibrillator is "E0617".
    the second defibrillator is furnished to Lou.
    the medical record of Lou documents myocardial infarction.
    the medical record of Lou documents coronary artery bypass graft within the past 3 months.
    the measured left ventricular ejection fraction of Lou is 0.25.
    the finding implantation surgery contraindicated about Lou is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    claim 3 is for the third defibrillator.
    the HCPCS code of the third defibrillator is "E0617".
    the third defibrillator is furnished to Max.
    the medical record of Max documents nonischemic dilated cardiomyopathy.
    the nonischemic dilated cardiomyopathy of Max was diagnosed on 2025-06-20.
    the order for the third defibrillator is dated 2026-02-20.
    the NYHA heart failure class of Max is 3.
    the measured left ventricular ejection fraction of Max is 0.30.
    the finding implantation surgery contraindicated about Max is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    claim 4 is for the fourth defibrillator.
    the HCPCS code of the fourth defibrillator is "E0617".
    the fourth defibrillator is furnished to Ned.
    the medical record of Ned documents ischemic dilated cardiomyopathy.
    the medical record of Ned documents myocardial infarction.
    the NYHA heart failure class of Ned is 4.
    the measured left ventricular ejection fraction of Ned is 0.20.
    the finding implantation surgery contraindicated about Ned is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 3 is reasonable and necessary", "claim 4 is reasonable and necessary"].

% Criterion B not decided: condition 1 met, nothing said about implantation
% surgery — the answer is conditional on that finding.
scenario implantation_not_decided is:
    claim 1 is for the defibrillator.
    the HCPCS code of the defibrillator is "E0617".
    the defibrillator is furnished to Oli.
    the medical record of Oli documents cardiac arrest due to ventricular fibrillation.
    the finding transient cause excluded about Oli is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"] and unknowns ["the finding implantation surgery contraindicated about Oli is established"].

% Replacement supplies (K0608) of a covered wearable defibrillator.
scenario wearable_supplies is:
    claim 1 is for the electrodes.
    the HCPCS code of the electrodes is "K0608".
    the electrodes is an accessory of the wearable defibrillator.
    the electrodes is furnished to Ann.
    the HCPCS code of the wearable defibrillator is "K0606".
    the wearable defibrillator is furnished to Ann.
    the medical record of Ann documents ventricular fibrillation.
    the finding transient cause excluded about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% Reasonable and necessary and fully documented, but the diagnosis code on
% the claim (I10, hypertension) is not in the article's list: payable fails
% at the remedy.
scenario diagnosis_code_not_listed is:
    claim 1 is for the wearable defibrillator.
    the HCPCS code of the wearable defibrillator is "K0606".
    the wearable defibrillator is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the medical record of Ann documents ventricular fibrillation.
    the finding transient cause excluded about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the diagnosis code of Ann is "I10".
    the order for the wearable defibrillator is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the wearable defibrillator is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the wearable defibrillator includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the wearable defibrillator includes order date.
    the order for the wearable defibrillator includes description of the item.
    the order for the wearable defibrillator includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the wearable defibrillator includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the wearable defibrillator was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the wearable defibrillator was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the wearable defibrillator.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at remedy"].

% Reasonable and necessary, but no proof of delivery: payable fails at the
% remedy; the proof flips it.
scenario no_proof_of_delivery is:
    claim 1 is for the wearable defibrillator.
    the HCPCS code of the wearable defibrillator is "K0606".
    the wearable defibrillator is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the medical record of Ann documents ventricular fibrillation.
    the finding transient cause excluded about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the diagnosis code of Ann is "I49.01".
    the order for the wearable defibrillator is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the wearable defibrillator is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the wearable defibrillator includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the wearable defibrillator includes order date.
    the order for the wearable defibrillator includes description of the item.
    the order for the wearable defibrillator includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the wearable defibrillator includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the wearable defibrillator was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the wearable defibrillator was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at remedy"].
    flip expects changes [["add: the supplier holds proof of delivery for the wearable defibrillator"]].
